First Author: Zhang
Title: Predictive accuracy of a perioperative hemodynamic indices-based prediction model for moderate-to-severe acute kidney injury after orthotopic heart transplantation
Source number: 79

Very short summary: This retrospective single-center cohort study included 114 adult orthotopic heart transplant recipients treated in China between 2011 and 2023, of whom 25 developed KDIGO stage 2–3 acute kidney injury within 7 days. Five machine-learning models were evaluated using five-fold cross-validation after univariate and LASSO feature selection; Light Gradient Boosting Machine performed best, with an AUC of 0.898, precision of 79.3%, F1-score of 0.722, AUPRC of 0.802, and Brier score of 0.106.

