	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: LGBM was compared with logistic regression, XGBoost, random forest, and Gaussian naïve Bayes. Candidate variables were first screened by univariate analysis and then by LASSO, leaving eight predictors: preoperative hemoglobin, PASP, left atrial dimension, aortic cross-clamp duration, intraoperative urine output, cumulative MAP below 65 mm Hg, post-CPB MAP area below 65 mm Hg, and post-CPB CVP above 20 mm Hg. Grid search with five-fold cross-validation was used for hyperparameter optimisation. SHAP summary and dependence plots were used for global and individual-level interpretation.

