	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Variables with more than 20% missingness were excluded, while remaining missing values were imputed using K-nearest-neighbour interpolation. Continuous variables underwent z-score normalization and categorical variables were one-hot encoded. Stage 2–3 AKI occurred in 25 of 114 recipients, but no class weighting, over-sampling, under-sampling, or other explicit imbalance strategy was reported. Five-fold cross-validation used four folds for training and one for validation, but exact fold-specific sample counts were not reported. Source code and trained model weights were not reported.

